From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:16:50 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): tool calls and results in session.transcript

session.transcript takes tool_details (chars, 0 = off; runtime.describe
lists transcript-tool-details-v1): an assistant row also lists its
tool_calls (id, name, arguments with each string cut to the bound) and is
kept when it has no text, and a tool row carries result (its stored text,
cut) and result_size. A reader can then show every call of a delegated
child with what it returned, also after the child ended; before, the rows
had no output and calls without text were dropped.

sessions.tool_outcome_metadata (false = off): each stored tool result also
carries display_metadata.tool_outcome, how long its call ran (duration_ms)
and whether it failed (is_error). The model never sees it.
